WEBVTT

00:00:06.670 --> 00:00:09.420
Shoot, Aerie!

00:00:09.590 --> 00:00:10.920
Fresh Waterspout!

00:00:18.350 --> 00:00:20.140
Look what you did!

00:00:22.350 --> 00:00:25.520
Don't let your guard down!

00:00:26.060 --> 00:00:27.730
Asahi!

00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:29.150
Wait!

00:00:29.360 --> 00:00:31.900
-You idiot!
-No!

00:00:32.070 --> 00:00:34.570
Now even Satsuki's messing around.

00:00:34.740 --> 00:00:36.410
Take that!

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:39.030
Don't just stand there acting so cold!

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:41.660
Haruto! You should join us!

00:00:41.830 --> 00:00:44.370
We didn't come here to play around.

00:00:44.540 --> 00:00:46.630
But we're at the ocean!

00:00:46.790 --> 00:00:49.630
And we don't have anything else to do.

00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:51.670
All right.

00:00:51.880 --> 00:00:53.670
Time to...

00:00:53.880 --> 00:00:55.430
get serious!

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:02.810
Hey! Go easy on us!

00:01:02.980 --> 00:01:06.730
I'm going to get serious too!

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:08.440
Okay!

00:01:08.650 --> 00:01:09.860
Bring it on!

00:01:10.020 --> 00:01:12.940
Hey! Take that!

00:01:32.090 --> 00:01:34.970
Seven Senses of the Re'Union

00:02:42.990 --> 00:02:47.910
Seeking the Sword

00:02:50.290 --> 00:02:53.000
Sorry to make you wait so long.

00:02:53.170 --> 00:02:55.130
No. We had fun!

00:02:55.300 --> 00:02:56.630
Fun?

00:02:56.800 --> 00:03:00.260
We played in the ocean until you came back to the port.

00:03:00.430 --> 00:03:02.970
Asahi, she doesn't need to know that!

00:03:04.100 --> 00:03:06.350
For making such a dangerous request,

00:03:06.520 --> 00:03:08.270
you're pretty relaxed.

00:03:08.430 --> 00:03:10.900
The people from the port told us that

00:03:11.060 --> 00:03:15.400
the only person who'd take on our request
is you, Ms. Alwida.

00:03:15.570 --> 00:03:17.030
Just call me Alwida.

00:03:17.190 --> 00:03:20.280
I don't like being so formal.

00:03:20.530 --> 00:03:22.410
The Lost Pentagon, huh?

00:03:22.570 --> 00:03:25.450
That place is pretty rough.

00:03:25.620 --> 00:03:26.990
Searching for a treasure?

00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:32.290
I heard a rumor there's an unbreakable sword
at the bottom of the sea in the Lost Pentagon.

00:03:32.460 --> 00:03:35.170
It's true, that sword exists.

00:03:35.340 --> 00:03:36.460
Really!?

00:03:36.630 --> 00:03:38.460
I heard this from someone who tried.

00:03:38.630 --> 00:03:42.130
The sword was thrust into the bottom of the sea
where it remains stuck.

00:03:42.300 --> 00:03:46.560
Most players lose before they ever get to the sword.

00:03:48.100 --> 00:03:50.060
I can see it over there.

00:03:51.060 --> 00:03:53.480
The Lost Pentagon.

00:04:02.780 --> 00:04:06.240
The area where the sword lies is around here.

00:04:06.780 --> 00:04:08.950
There's no wind, so there are no waves.

00:04:09.120 --> 00:04:10.750
Nor any signs of fish.

00:04:10.910 --> 00:04:14.540
It's a no-man's land.

00:04:17.130 --> 00:04:19.420
Master Haruto!

00:04:19.590 --> 00:04:22.720
You'll get worn out underwater.

00:04:22.880 --> 00:04:26.930
A lot of players don't consider the trip back
and end up dying here.

00:04:27.100 --> 00:04:29.310
Don't overdo it.

00:04:29.470 --> 00:04:30.770
I got it.

00:04:30.930 --> 00:04:33.810
If the boat is in danger, retreat from this place.

00:04:33.980 --> 00:04:36.150
We'll take care of ourselves.

00:04:38.150 --> 00:04:40.440
Protect those two.

00:04:40.610 --> 00:04:42.240
They're not the type to stay quiet

00:04:42.400 --> 00:04:44.410
and let me protect them.

00:05:19.650 --> 00:05:23.940
EQUIPMENT

00:05:39.500 --> 00:05:42.760
It's not easy to find.

00:05:42.920 --> 00:05:46.470
And there's a time limit on how long
we can stay underwater.

00:05:46.630 --> 00:05:49.010
And the search area is too large.

00:05:49.180 --> 00:05:51.640
It's a test of endurance.

00:05:51.810 --> 00:05:56.270
We'll just have to look everywhere,
even if it takes a long time.

00:05:56.440 --> 00:05:57.980
Hey.

00:05:59.610 --> 00:06:01.110
I feel like it's...

00:06:01.320 --> 00:06:03.110
that way.

00:06:03.650 --> 00:06:06.110
"Feel like"? That's a bit vague.

00:06:06.650 --> 00:06:07.860
So what?

00:06:08.030 --> 00:06:10.660
We have to look everywhere anyway.

00:06:10.820 --> 00:06:13.370
Let's take a look.

00:06:15.040 --> 00:06:17.500
There's nothing here...

00:06:26.970 --> 00:06:28.510
No way...

00:06:30.720 --> 00:06:32.010
Why...?

00:06:34.680 --> 00:06:36.270
It's Pleiades!

00:06:36.430 --> 00:06:40.020
Maybe it's just the same design...

00:06:40.190 --> 00:06:41.480
No...

00:06:42.310 --> 00:06:44.980
My Fighting Sense is telling me...

00:06:46.150 --> 00:06:48.860
That sword's my pal.

00:06:50.410 --> 00:06:52.950
Haruto, pull it out, quick!

00:06:53.120 --> 00:06:54.700
Okay.

00:07:13.470 --> 00:07:15.260
An earthquake!?

00:07:39.330 --> 00:07:41.330
The King of the Dead Sea, Aegir!

00:07:42.120 --> 00:07:43.330
You know about it?

00:07:43.500 --> 00:07:45.670
The rumors say that a huge monster

00:07:45.840 --> 00:07:48.420
with that name hides in the sea.

00:07:50.340 --> 00:07:52.050
Look!

00:07:56.850 --> 00:07:58.640
No way...

00:08:00.060 --> 00:08:02.600
FANTASY MARCH
GLORY SPECTRAL

00:08:02.850 --> 00:08:04.900
NOZOMI KUSAKA

00:08:24.170 --> 00:08:25.710
Haruto!

00:08:55.320 --> 00:08:57.320
Clive!

00:09:23.600 --> 00:09:26.400
Well, well. That was a strong opponent.

00:09:26.560 --> 00:09:30.480
Who knew fighting underwater would be so hard?

00:09:30.900 --> 00:09:32.900
Huh? Where's Clive?

00:09:33.110 --> 00:09:35.990
He was with us when we escaped to the surface.

00:09:36.150 --> 00:09:39.990
I hope he didn't get separated from us and drown!

00:09:46.370 --> 00:09:49.420
I have something to do.
See you next time.

00:09:49.580 --> 00:09:52.130
-Is that all?
-He left a letter?

00:09:52.300 --> 00:09:54.720
If it was an e-mail, we could have sent a reply.

00:09:54.880 --> 00:09:58.680
He's not the type to feel shy
about seeing us again after a long time.

00:09:58.890 --> 00:10:02.760
Being indirect like this
is so typical of Clive!

00:10:02.970 --> 00:10:06.140
He's always been someone who
does things at his own pace.

00:10:06.810 --> 00:10:09.440
I feel relieved now.

00:10:11.980 --> 00:10:15.400
MEMORY

00:10:20.490 --> 00:10:22.490
There's a lot of people here...

00:10:22.660 --> 00:10:25.200
The guilds united to beat Subaru.

00:10:25.370 --> 00:10:26.910
That's so immature.

00:10:27.120 --> 00:10:30.500
Should we apologize?

00:10:30.670 --> 00:10:32.540
Why do we have to apologize!?

00:10:32.710 --> 00:10:33.960
Well...

00:10:34.130 --> 00:10:36.550
We stole the boss from them.

00:10:36.760 --> 00:10:39.970
We haven't done anything against the rules.

00:10:40.140 --> 00:10:43.510
We just defeated a boss they couldn't defeat themselves.

00:10:43.680 --> 00:10:45.720
But, they announced that

00:10:45.890 --> 00:10:48.810
they were going to be the first to beat it.

00:10:52.060 --> 00:10:54.070
This is where we make our exit.

00:10:55.780 --> 00:10:57.070
I'm leaving.

00:10:57.280 --> 00:10:59.200
-What!?
-What do you mean!?

00:11:00.610 --> 00:11:02.070
I'm leaving Subaru.

00:11:02.280 --> 00:11:03.370
Huh!?

00:11:03.530 --> 00:11:05.410
We can't win.

00:11:06.040 --> 00:11:07.700
It's better to surrender now

00:11:07.870 --> 00:11:09.410
to avoid getting hurt.

00:11:09.580 --> 00:11:10.830
You're making a mistake!

00:11:11.040 --> 00:11:12.960
I don't want to get a game over.

00:11:13.130 --> 00:11:15.340
And I'm not the type to stay indoors forever.

00:11:15.500 --> 00:11:16.630
Are you serious?

00:11:16.800 --> 00:11:19.170
Have I ever lied to you?

00:11:19.340 --> 00:11:20.970
Many times.

00:11:21.130 --> 00:11:23.680
But this time, I'm telling the truth.

00:11:23.850 --> 00:11:25.850
And I

00:11:26.390 --> 00:11:29.810
wanted to try fighting against Subaru once.

00:11:34.690 --> 00:11:36.860
You're Mr. Amo and Ms. Usui, right?

00:11:38.490 --> 00:11:39.990
This way.

00:11:43.450 --> 00:11:44.620
You came.

00:11:45.910 --> 00:11:47.740
You can order anything.

00:11:48.290 --> 00:11:49.870
I'll treat you.

00:11:50.040 --> 00:11:52.290
Oh. You're so generous.

00:11:52.460 --> 00:11:54.750
I'm the one who invited you out.

00:11:54.920 --> 00:11:56.290
It's nothing.

00:11:56.460 --> 00:11:59.340
Then I'll have an iced café au lait.

00:11:59.510 --> 00:12:01.880
I'll have a marron chocolat,

00:12:02.470 --> 00:12:04.390
a shortcake, a Sachertorte,

00:12:04.550 --> 00:12:07.350
a chiffon cake, and a strawberry tart.

00:12:07.510 --> 00:12:09.140
And some Darjeeling tea.

00:12:10.310 --> 00:12:12.020
I'll have that hot, please.

00:12:12.190 --> 00:12:13.650
Yes, madam.

00:12:13.810 --> 00:12:15.310
Hey. Satsuki!?

00:12:15.480 --> 00:12:19.150
I thought you had more self-restraint.

00:12:19.360 --> 00:12:23.320
What? Did you forget that you almost

00:12:23.490 --> 00:12:26.030
made me get a game over?

00:12:26.200 --> 00:12:27.580
Well, that was...

00:12:27.740 --> 00:12:30.160
Now we can call it even.

00:12:30.660 --> 00:12:32.620
But we haven't even had lunch yet!

00:12:32.790 --> 00:12:34.880
Do you know how many calories--?

00:12:37.130 --> 00:12:38.800
Do you have a problem with that!?

00:12:38.960 --> 00:12:41.170
No! It's nothing!

00:12:42.130 --> 00:12:44.430
What's so funny?

00:12:54.310 --> 00:12:55.520
Delicious!

00:12:55.690 --> 00:12:58.650
This tart isn't overly sweet! It's so elegant!

00:12:58.820 --> 00:13:00.730
Your father's hotel

00:13:00.900 --> 00:13:03.200
really deserves its reputation!

00:13:03.820 --> 00:13:05.950
Thanks.

00:13:07.490 --> 00:13:09.120
So...

00:13:09.280 --> 00:13:11.330
You have something you wanted to tell us?

00:13:12.120 --> 00:13:13.460
I'm not free all day either,

00:13:13.620 --> 00:13:14.870
so down to business.

00:13:15.080 --> 00:13:17.580
Of course,
it's about Asahi.

00:13:18.130 --> 00:13:19.540
After Asahi came back,

00:13:19.710 --> 00:13:22.630
didn't you feel anything unnatural?

00:13:23.590 --> 00:13:25.260
One thing that comes to mind

00:13:25.430 --> 00:13:28.220
is that rumors started spreading so fast.

00:13:28.760 --> 00:13:31.220
So fast that it was unnatural.

00:13:32.470 --> 00:13:34.980
You finally caught on.

00:13:35.140 --> 00:13:37.600
Gnosis is pulling the strings
behind the scenes.

00:13:38.150 --> 00:13:39.520
Did you say Gnosis!?

00:13:39.690 --> 00:13:42.190
One of the high guilds that's been around
since Union?

00:13:42.400 --> 00:13:43.610
I remember them.

00:13:43.780 --> 00:13:46.320
They're really secretive and shady.

00:13:47.200 --> 00:13:51.330
There was a group who tried to find out
what Gnosis's secret was.

00:13:51.540 --> 00:13:54.580
They all got erased from Re'Union.

00:13:55.080 --> 00:13:56.210
Erased?

00:13:56.410 --> 00:13:57.710
Do you mean...

00:13:58.250 --> 00:14:01.000
The logs were erased too,

00:14:01.170 --> 00:14:04.300
so almost no one knows it ever happened.

00:14:04.460 --> 00:14:06.840
How did they do that?

00:14:07.010 --> 00:14:09.430
When I found out about it,

00:14:09.590 --> 00:14:13.600
I checked with the players who got game over in the real
world,

00:14:13.770 --> 00:14:16.940
but no one would tell me anything.

00:14:17.100 --> 00:14:20.730
I don't like to think that
a guild in a virtual world

00:14:20.900 --> 00:14:22.690
has so much influence over reality.

00:14:23.230 --> 00:14:25.820
Why are they after Asahi!?

00:14:26.400 --> 00:14:28.570
I don't know.

00:14:29.360 --> 00:14:31.990
Some people want the glory of beating Asahi,

00:14:32.160 --> 00:14:34.700
and other people want her power.

00:14:34.870 --> 00:14:38.620
There's no consistency in their goals.

00:14:38.790 --> 00:14:43.840
The reason Southern Cross
and the Brill Society betrayed me and formed Divine

00:14:44.050 --> 00:14:46.420
was because of Gnosis's secret work.

00:14:46.590 --> 00:14:48.340
That's what I think.

00:14:48.510 --> 00:14:50.090
So, you're saying

00:14:50.260 --> 00:14:53.100
Gnosis did that to
get others to go after Asahi!?

00:14:53.930 --> 00:14:56.100
I don't want Asahi to find about this.

00:14:56.270 --> 00:14:59.350
I don't want to make her worry.

00:14:59.940 --> 00:15:01.190
And that's why

00:15:01.350 --> 00:15:03.360
you invited us here.

00:15:03.900 --> 00:15:04.980
I feel reluctant,

00:15:05.150 --> 00:15:06.650
but I thought

00:15:06.820 --> 00:15:09.490
I should tell the people who are with her.

00:15:10.360 --> 00:15:12.870
That's all I can say.

00:15:13.450 --> 00:15:17.370
We also have something to tell you.

00:15:18.080 --> 00:15:19.500
We met Clive.

00:15:19.660 --> 00:15:21.000
Clive!?

00:15:22.290 --> 00:15:23.630
Anyways...

00:15:23.840 --> 00:15:26.960
We haven't been able to
get in touch with him since then.

00:15:27.130 --> 00:15:30.380
What's he doing sneaking around?

00:15:30.550 --> 00:15:32.090
Regardless of Clive,

00:15:32.260 --> 00:15:36.720
it's hard to believe that story about Pleiades
being thrust into Aegir.

00:15:36.890 --> 00:15:38.310
Yeah.

00:15:38.480 --> 00:15:40.560
The moment we logged into Re'Union,

00:15:40.730 --> 00:15:44.310
all our old equipment was gone.

00:15:44.480 --> 00:15:46.980
When I grasped it, I was sure.

00:15:47.900 --> 00:15:50.030
It was definitely

00:15:50.200 --> 00:15:51.360
my sword.

00:15:52.700 --> 00:15:55.950
But Haruto, you picked up Subaru's party ring, right?

00:15:56.450 --> 00:15:58.290
I just dropped it for some reason,

00:15:58.450 --> 00:16:02.370
and it remained on the field as an item. But...

00:16:03.630 --> 00:16:05.880
Pleiades was always mine.

00:16:09.210 --> 00:16:11.010
Until the last moment...

00:16:13.220 --> 00:16:15.350
There's lots of things I don't understand.

00:16:15.510 --> 00:16:17.310
But, the key to all this

00:16:17.470 --> 00:16:19.520
is that red stone.

00:16:19.720 --> 00:16:21.020
Maybe it's related

00:16:21.180 --> 00:16:23.900
to the strange visions the stone shows us.

00:16:24.400 --> 00:16:26.110
Ever since I saw that,

00:16:26.270 --> 00:16:28.690
I've been thinking.

00:16:29.030 --> 00:16:31.400
I came up with a hypothesis.

00:16:31.900 --> 00:16:32.900
A hypothesis?

00:16:33.530 --> 00:16:34.860
Asahi's body

00:16:35.030 --> 00:16:37.830
might exist in

00:16:37.990 --> 00:16:39.160
the real world.

00:16:40.580 --> 00:16:42.540
Do you have any idea what you're saying!?

00:16:42.750 --> 00:16:44.670
I know!

00:16:45.580 --> 00:16:48.290
But, that vision the stone showed us...

00:16:49.210 --> 00:16:52.050
If that vision is from the real world...

00:16:52.630 --> 00:16:53.880
If so,

00:16:54.050 --> 00:16:57.050
then Asahi is probably... No.

00:16:57.600 --> 00:16:59.220
I'll stop here.

00:16:59.390 --> 00:17:01.890
It's outrageous.

00:17:02.060 --> 00:17:03.640
Sorry. Forget about it.

00:17:03.810 --> 00:17:05.810
It's been a while.

00:17:07.230 --> 00:17:09.440
Mr. Haruto, and Ms. Satsuki.

00:17:09.940 --> 00:17:11.150
Hello.

00:17:11.320 --> 00:17:13.530
It's nice to see you, Secretary.

00:17:13.700 --> 00:17:15.700
You haven't changed at all.

00:17:16.240 --> 00:17:18.450
You two have grown up so much!

00:17:18.660 --> 00:17:21.410
Just state your business.

00:17:21.580 --> 00:17:24.330
I've discovered the whereabouts of Nozomi Kusaka.

00:17:27.420 --> 00:17:28.920
Don't say that here!

00:17:29.090 --> 00:17:30.170
Is there a problem?

00:17:30.340 --> 00:17:31.380
There's a big problem!

00:17:31.550 --> 00:17:34.420
You were searching for Nozomi?

00:17:34.590 --> 00:17:38.340
I thought you were against reviving Subaru!

00:17:38.510 --> 00:17:39.800
Don't get the wrong idea.

00:17:39.970 --> 00:17:41.890
It was Asahi's wish.

00:17:42.060 --> 00:17:43.810
I didn't do it for you!

00:17:43.980 --> 00:17:46.060
So, where is Nozomi?

00:17:46.270 --> 00:17:47.810
I have good news.

00:17:47.980 --> 00:17:50.690
She's returned to this city.

00:17:57.360 --> 00:17:59.200
After all that happened,

00:17:59.410 --> 00:18:01.580
you're trying again?

00:18:01.790 --> 00:18:03.540
Where there's treasure,

00:18:03.700 --> 00:18:06.660
Subaru will go!

00:18:06.830 --> 00:18:08.750
You have a lot of spirit!

00:18:08.920 --> 00:18:10.460
I admire you.

00:18:14.380 --> 00:18:15.470
Welcome back.

00:18:16.010 --> 00:18:18.720
How many times have we dived already?

00:18:18.930 --> 00:18:21.220
We have to start over.

00:18:21.390 --> 00:18:23.850
I feel like giving up.

00:18:24.770 --> 00:18:26.730
Alwida? What's wrong?

00:18:29.940 --> 00:18:31.110
Clive!?

00:18:31.270 --> 00:18:34.110
Hey. I haven't seen you three since yesterday.

00:18:35.240 --> 00:18:37.610
Do you need my help?

00:18:41.990 --> 00:18:43.120
What's wrong?

00:18:43.330 --> 00:18:45.620
We haven't seen each other for so long!

00:18:46.160 --> 00:18:48.920
You are Clive, right?

00:18:49.080 --> 00:18:50.500
Come on now.

00:18:50.670 --> 00:18:53.130
Who else would I be?

00:18:54.170 --> 00:18:55.420
You are Clive!

00:18:55.590 --> 00:18:57.300
What have you been doing?

00:18:57.880 --> 00:19:01.050
It's a long story.
Let's talk after our work is done.

00:19:04.310 --> 00:19:05.310
What's that?

00:19:05.520 --> 00:19:09.020
It's an item that stops enemies from appearing.

00:19:09.190 --> 00:19:11.310
I used some up yesterday.

00:19:11.520 --> 00:19:13.310
So... You too?

00:19:13.860 --> 00:19:17.240
Yeah. I'm after Aegir too.

00:19:17.400 --> 00:19:21.240
and then I came across you all by chance.

00:19:21.410 --> 00:19:24.330
I see. I was surprised!

00:19:24.490 --> 00:19:27.000
You can say the same for both of us!

00:19:27.160 --> 00:19:28.370
How have you been?

00:19:28.540 --> 00:19:29.960
Good!

00:19:31.330 --> 00:19:33.920
Well... Let's begin.

00:19:40.300 --> 00:19:42.010
What?

00:19:42.180 --> 00:19:43.260
Let's go.

00:19:43.430 --> 00:19:46.180
It should have appeared by now.

00:19:52.310 --> 00:19:54.480
Now we can move freely.

00:19:55.020 --> 00:19:59.860
It's a collaboration between Clive's shapeshifting
and my magic. Just like old times.

00:20:10.330 --> 00:20:11.960
There it is!

